<https://github.com/john1hsu/ai-knowledge-graph/id/an-image-is-worth-16x16-words> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The ICLR 2021 paper by Dosovitskiy and eleven Google Research colleagues that introduced the Vision Transformer (ViT): it cuts an image into fixed-size patches, embeds each patch as a token and feeds the sequence to a nearly unmodified Transformer encoder, showing that with enough pre-training data this convolution-free model matches or beats state-of-the-art CNNs at lower pre-training compute." .
